{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Quaternion Rotation in Blender.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Quaternion Rotation in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"quaternion rotation in blender quaternion rotation in blender","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Quaternion Rotation in Blender.md","fileName":"Quaternion Rotation in Blender.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Quaternion Rotation in Blender","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-07 23:25\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Keyframe Animation and Rigging]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Keyframe Animation and Rigging","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Quaternion Rotation in Blender.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Quaternion Rotation in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"quaternion rotation in blender quaternion rotation in blender","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Quaternion Rotation in Blender.md","fileName":"Quaternion Rotation in Blender.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Quaternion Rotation in Blender","heading":"Quaternion Rotation in Blender","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Quaternion rotation represents orientation with four animation channels rather than the three X, Y, and Z channels of Euler rotation. Blender commonly uses it for bones because it avoids the gimbal-lock failure that can prevent an Euler system from expressing a needed rotation.\n\nThe tradeoff is interpretation: quaternion values do not correspond intuitively to separate axis angles. They are reliable for interpolation but often less convenient for an animator to edit directly in the Graph Editor.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Keyframe Animation and Rigging","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":"